I18N[amnezia_err_ipacket_program_only]="%s rejected: only the amneziawg-go program understands the <%s> tag — routers and Linux with the AmneziaWG kernel module will not connect with such an I. Use tags every client understands: b, t, r, rc, rd."
I18N[amnezia_warn_ipacket_kernel_only]="%s contains <%s> — only the AmneziaWG kernel module understands it; AmneziaVPN clients on phones will not connect with such an %s. Replace %s via «Change a single parameter» on the profile card (in the panel — «Obfuscation parameters» → «Change a parameter»)."
I18N[amnezia_warn_ipacket_program_only]="%s contains <%s> — only the amneziawg-go program understands it; routers and Linux with the AmneziaWG kernel module will not connect with such an %s. Replace %s via «Change a single parameter» on the profile card (in the panel — «Obfuscation parameters» → «Change a parameter»)."
I18N[amnezia_err_ipacket_too_big]="%s rejected: the packet comes out at %s bytes, the limit is 1280. It will not pass without fragmentation, and a huge I makes awg show loop on the kernel module."
