# DUP-LINE-01 (owner's decision 15.10): no 2.0 on the server — old clients cannot connect; our own line duplicates the
# one adopted from the app — «Move to 2.0» (our own profile only; the app's profile is never touched).
I18N[amnezia_dupline_text]="There is no AmneziaWG 2.0 on the server: old app versions (AmneziaVPN before 5.0.1.5, DefaultVPN) cannot connect to 3.1, and Keenetic routers on regular firmware connect only to AmneziaWG 1.5 or 1.0 if it is installed (Keenetic understands 3.1 only in dev firmware so far). The fix moves %s to 2.0: the port and subnet stay. goAmnezia pro issues new keys to the users on it (%s) right away. A subscription picks them up by itself only where the app refreshes it by itself; the connection page has to be opened again and the new key imported, and those who were sent the key or file by hand have to scan the QR code or import the key again: the old one stops working. The app's profile is not touched."
I18N[amnezia_dupline_text_nobody]="There is no AmneziaWG 2.0 on the server: old app versions (AmneziaVPN before 5.0.1.5, DefaultVPN) cannot connect to 3.1, and Keenetic routers on regular firmware connect only to AmneziaWG 1.5 or 1.0 if it is installed (Keenetic understands 3.1 only in dev firmware so far). The fix moves %s to 2.0: the port and subnet stay. There are no users on it. The app's profile is not touched."
I18N[amnezia_lines_no20]="There is no AmneziaWG 2.0 on the server: old app versions (AmneziaVPN before 5.0.1.5, DefaultVPN) and Keenetic routers on regular firmware cannot connect to any profile (Keenetic understands 3.1 only in dev firmware so far)."
