# 1.0.13 — limits of what we write (live checks 08.10, PARAM-03, 05, 08, 09): a refused write (err) and an adoption
# warning (warn). Numbers and corridors — lib/awgkeys.py (limit_problems).
I18N[amnezia_err_corridor]="%s = %s rejected: allowed from %s to %s (new profiles get %s). %s"
I18N[amnezia_warn_corridor]="%s = %s — outside the corridor %s–%s (new profiles get %s). %s Fix it via «Change a single parameter» on the profile card."
I18N[amnezia_corridor_why_rekey_after]="It is how often, in seconds, the session key is replaced: less often — the key dies before it is replaced and the connection drops for seconds, and a very large number AmneziaWG does not accept at all — the profile will not come up; more often — extra handshakes."
I18N[amnezia_corridor_why_rekey_timeout]="It is the pause between handshake attempts, in seconds: below 3 — a flood of handshakes (live, 0-7 gave 16.5 times more packets)."
I18N[amnezia_corridor_why_reject_after]="It is when the session key dies, in seconds: the AmneziaWG kernel module keeps it no longer than 180 s, and below 150 the key dies before it is replaced."
I18N[amnezia_corridor_why_keepalive]="It is after how many seconds an empty packet answers: below 5 — empty packets almost at once, above 15 — extra handshakes."
I18N[amnezia_corridor_why_handshakes]="It is how many handshake attempts are made before giving up: below 10 — it gives up at the first network glitch, above 30 — minutes of useless attempts."
I18N[amnezia_corridor_why_padding]="It is padding added to data packets, in bytes: it never makes a packet larger than 1400 anyway, and a number above 65535 the kernel module silently truncates (live, 70000 became 4464), so the two sides disagree."
I18N[amnezia_err_timing_order]="%s = %s rejected: a new session key would be requested only after %s s (RejectAfterTime − KeepaliveTimeout − RekeyTimeout), while RekeyAfterTime of the profile goes up to %s s: the key would die before it is replaced, and the connection would drop for seconds. First put back into the corridor: %s."
I18N[amnezia_err_timing_order_plain]="%s = %s rejected: a new session key would be requested only after %s s (RejectAfterTime − KeepaliveTimeout − RekeyTimeout), while RekeyAfterTime of the profile goes up to %s s: the key would die before it is replaced, and the connection would drop for seconds."
I18N[amnezia_warn_timing_order]="3.1 timings: a new session key is requested only after %s s (RejectAfterTime − KeepaliveTimeout − RekeyTimeout), while RekeyAfterTime goes up to %s s: the key dies before it is replaced, and the connection drops for seconds. Put back into the corridor: %s."
I18N[amnezia_err_junk_burst]="%s = %s rejected: every handshake attempt would be preceded by Jc × Jmax = %s × %s = %s bytes of junk — more than %s (16 KB). On a weak upload the handshake stretches to seconds (live, Jc 122 × Jmax 1280 at 1 Mbit/s — 6.7 s instead of 0.09). Lower Jc or Jmax: new profiles get 4–6 packets of 10–50 bytes."
I18N[amnezia_warn_junk_burst]="Jc × Jmax = %s × %s = %s bytes of junk before every handshake attempt — more than %s (16 KB): on a weak upload the handshake stretches to seconds. Lower Jc or Jmax via «Change a single parameter» on the profile card."
I18N[amnezia_err_jc_ipackets]="%s = %s rejected: Jc + the number of set I1–I5 = %s + %s = %s, and clients on the amneziawg-go program (the AmneziaVPN app on phones) come up only while it is at most %s — their keys would not connect with such a set («Protocol error»). Lower Jc."
I18N[amnezia_warn_jc_ipackets]="Jc + the number of set I1–I5 = %s + %s = %s — more than %s: clients on the amneziawg-go program (the AmneziaVPN app on phones) will not connect with such a set («Protocol error»). Lower Jc via «Change a single parameter» on the profile card."
I18N[amnezia_err_trailers_loss]="%s = %s rejected: with trailers (RandomTrailers) different S (%s while S4 = %s) and wide H (%s — %s values together) make the receiver take about 1 in %s data packets for a handshake and drop it (live, 6.5 %% of packets were lost). Make those S equal to S4, or those H single numbers, or turn RandomTrailers off."
I18N[amnezia_warn_trailers_loss]="With trailers (RandomTrailers) different S (%s while S4 = %s) and wide H (%s — %s values together): the receiver takes about 1 in %s data packets for a handshake and drops it (live, 6.5 %% loss). Make those S equal to S4, or those H single numbers, or turn RandomTrailers off via «Change a single parameter» on the profile card."
